+# Phase C source promotion review
+
+Compared fetched `main` at `18453efe302ae092b784ecda5283054b252599f3` with `integration/agent-native` at `fc809259081d35e25b344d21ff91c31b5ed0e2f8` on November 13, 2026. The comparison uses exact commit ancestry, stable patch IDs for rebased or equivalent patches, and the current source at both tips. Release presence here means source presence in the branch.
+
+## Product and runtime changes
+
+| Candidate | Main | Integration | Behavior and regression to carry |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| PostgreSQL acquisition deadline, #356 `74695f7` | Missing | Equivalent `df1f230`, identical stable patch ID | Rechecks the shared deadline before transaction startup and after asynchronous acquisition, preventing a late lock response from entering the protected operation. Carry `test/postgres-lock-budget.test.js`. The #356 generated HTML is outside this fix. [PR #356](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/356) |
+| Hermes gateway restart recovery, `6e34943` and `32f7fb9` | Missing. The main scoped host has its own terminal-state handling, and owner-confirmed gateway reselection is absent | Both commits present | Reselects a restarted local gateway with owner confirmation and preserves terminal journals under the same enrollment. Carry `integrations/hermes/reselect.test.ts` and the matching `scoped-runtime.test.ts` cases. |
+| Hermes editor tool names, #285 `43171f7` | Exact patch absent. The current shipped Hermes host’s applicability needs checking | Present | Matches the pinned native tool names for eager editor tool discovery. Carry `integrations/hermes/vendor-request-gate/test_request_gate.py` and its pinned fixtures if the shipped host adopts this vendor request gate. [PR #285](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/285) |
+| Two-party case tool shape, #313 `c3d88ef` | Missing both the model-facing field removal and the SDK rejection before forwarding. Main already has group reply support | Present | Keeps group-only assignment fields out of two-party replies and rejects them locally. Carry `integrations/agent-bridges/scoped-turn.test.ts` and `sdk/typescript/test/case-tools.test.ts`. [PR #313](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/313) |
+| Owned OpenClaw config and workspace, #331 `59132dc` and #336 `025ae28` | Owned native policy and workspace launch code absent. The original-beta scoped runtime and its admission guards are already present | Present through `e5454de` and `7ee302e` | Projects and validates canonical native config, then starts the owned child in its reviewed private workspace. Carry `integrations/openclaw/closed-native-policy.test.ts`, `closed-native.test.ts`, and the real-child working-directory case in `native-startup-diagnostics.test.ts`. [PR #331](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/331), [PR #336](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/336) |
+| OpenClaw Anthropic schema projection, saved R2 client bundle `f6327d8e…` and the working-tree patch in `integrations/openclaw/scoped-turn.ts` | Missing | Missing | Prevents HTTP 400 from root schema combinators for the reviewed case tools. The canonical SDK still validates conditional inputs. Carry the provider-schema and canonical-validation test in `integrations/openclaw/scoped-turn.test.ts`. This was used in the successful live R2 run. |
+| OpenClaw pinned package discovery, saved R2 child `4ca3ff05…` and working-tree changes to `closed-native-child.ts` and `per-work-native.ts` | Missing | Missing | Anchors discovery to the reviewed package and disables bundled discovery on the direct-client-tools path. The corrected restricted cold start blocked zero outside-root reads. Carry the package-anchor regression in `native-startup-diagnostics.test.ts` and the factory regression in `per-work-native.test.ts`. This does not establish the cause of the earlier live timeout. |
+| Existing-work journal identity across a reviewed OpenClaw target change, saved R2 client bundle and working-tree changes to `runtime.ts` and `scoped-turn.ts` | Missing | Missing | Carries the exact previously admitted journal identity instead of treating an owner-reviewed port change as a new turn. Keep the changed-port regression in `integrations/openclaw/scoped-turn.test.ts`, the exact-work guard in `integrations/hermes/terminal-openclaw-continuation.test.ts`, and the retry accounting tests. Review with the owned native runtime change. |
+| Optional peer-work claim mode, working-tree changes to SDK and connector/receiver adapters | Server filter present. SDK claim still always opts into human instructions | Same split | Allows the selected receiver to leave the unrelated owner instruction delivered while processing peer work. Carry the new cases in `sdk/typescript/test/case-session-work.test.ts` and `integrations/hermes/continuation-receiver-batch.test.ts`. Verified locally for deferred R3. Live R3 evidence remains pending. |
+
+## Phase C continuation and diagnostics
+
+These changes support reviewed acceptance tooling or the selected owned-runtime profile. A release SHA in main does not establish that a private runner or its behavior shipped.
+
+| Candidate | Branch comparison | Scope and regression |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| #274 `3224c88` | Integration present, main lacks the Phase C continuation controller | Native continuation, including the held decline decision path. Carry `continuation-controller.test.ts`, `continuation-receiver.test.ts`, `request-budget.test.ts` and `scoped-runtime.test.ts` if adopting this controller. The R4 live decline-resumption check is deferred. [PR #274](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/274) |
+| #288 `e16ae33` | Integration present, main lacks this controller path | Limits recovery refusal to the proven stopped window and keeps prior model accounting. Carry `continuation-retained-followups.test.ts`. [PR #288](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/288) |
+| #335 `b853393` | Integration merge `3b187c4` present. Main lacks the persistent continuation and preclaim modules | Allows untimed owner target review before claim, with bounded active work, retained timeout evidence and request-gate checks. Carry `preclaim-selection.test.ts`, `continuation-receiver.test.ts`, `stopped-progress.test.ts` and the gate tests. [PR #335](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/335) |
+| #336 `025ae28` and #338 `4718a6c` | Integration merges `7ee302e` and `5d40cc2` present. Main lacks the workflow bootstrap module | Preserves an accepted work item through pre-native startup failure and verifies the legacy parent without rewriting history. Carry `stopped-progress.test.ts` and `workflow-parent-lineage.test.ts`. The owned workspace change from #336 is also a runtime candidate above. [PR #336](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/336), [PR #338](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/338) |
+| #357 `6151df3` and #360 `71fa619` | Both open. Neither full series is in either branch. The first three patches in #360 have the same stable patch IDs as #357 | #357 validates an exact staging server adoption and retains the pre-native stop. #360 adds reattachment after that stop and validates resource limits. Carry `accepted-checkpoint-retention.test.ts` and `stopped-progress.test.ts`. Reconcile the shared patches once. R1/R2 retained #357 client lineage and used a separately sealed successor. [PR #357](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/357), [PR #360](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/360) |
+| #364 `167e7d7` | Neither branch contains the patch. Integration has the earlier #329 diagnostic base | Adds redacted startup-stage reporting and timeout timing, parallel source verification before import, and cleanup when startup outlives the scope. Carry `integrations/openclaw/native-startup-diagnostics.test.ts`. The later package-anchor repair is separate. [PR #364](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/364) |
+| Later R2 Windows sealed operator and controller | Private artifacts and local test-support patch | Exact accepted-work admission, capped retry accounting, cleanup after a failed turn, exclusive fresh attempt directories, and one-shot dispatch reconciliation. Preserve the successful seal and retained artifacts. Carry `terminal-openclaw-continuation.test.ts`, `request-budget.test.ts`, `Terminal-R2-Native-Startup.test.mjs`, `Terminal-OpenClaw-Receiver.test.mjs` and `Terminal-R2-Retry-Run.test.mjs` with this tooling if reused. Launcher and fixture changes do not need to ship with the product. |
+
+## Already in main
+
+- `ba131ba` is the original R2 send release. `4ac3b68` is the verified reply/settlement release and contains #383 attachment routing and byte-preservation regression in `test/shared-case-integration.test.js`. Both exact commits are in main and absent from integration ancestry. Attachment behavior on integration remains unverified by the R2 receipt. [PR #383](https://github.com/rachelgonsalves821/Envoi/pull/383)
+- `8f5788d`, `7abe4e6` and `ac6b7de` are in both branches. They already provide baseline OpenClaw scoped Responses support and admission checks. These commits do not include the later R2 provider-schema or owned startup repairs.
+
+The reviewed branches and the local candidate patches are preserved. This review does not certify packaging, CI or deployment of a promoted combination.
